        "original_id": "54b09d89-95de-5f55-95b8-55bc9c1fb5b2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arthur Sullivan, Vincenzo Bellini\n- Works: L'Île Enchantée, La Sonnambula\n- Places: Covent Garden\n- Topics: ballet, divertissement, compositions\n\nFacts:\n- In 1864, Arthur Sullivan wrote the ballet L'Île Enchantée.\n- L'Île Enchantée means The Enchanted Island.\n- Arthur Sullivan wrote L'Île Enchantée as a divertissement to be performed at the end of Vincenzo Bellini's La Sonnambula at Covent Garden.\n- Arthur Sullivan's body of work includes 23 operas, 13 major orchestral works, eight choral works and oratorios, two ballets, incidental music to several plays, numerous hymns and other church pieces, songs, and piano and chamber pieces.",
